@*
    Row 33 of the parity inventory: a page switch for draw.io's own rulers. The inventory measured
    that setRulerVisible exists on draw.io's EditorUi but no menu reaches it with ui=min - this
    component is that missing menu, and it is only the SHOWN half of the feature: it holds no
    localStorage and no reference to draw.io itself, both of which live in drawio-bridge.js
    (setRulerVisible, loadRulerPreference, saveRulerPreference) - the one place this page already
    keeps everything that touches draw.io's ui and the browser's own storage. This component only
    shows what Enabled says and reports a click through OnToggle; DrawioEditor.razor is what carries
    the answer to and from the bridge.
*@
@* In the page's bar since the passata grafica (2026-09-29): an icon button, lit while the rulers are
   on. It is still a checkbox, and the checkbox is still what is pressed: transparent, it lies over
   the whole of the icon (see .drawio-ruler-switch in wcs-webeditor.css), so the mouse, the keyboard
   and a test's click all reach the <input> itself - the icon and the tip are only what is seen.
   "Rulers" is the checkbox's name (aria-label: the tip is not shown, so it names nothing) and the
   tip the mouse or the focus opens. The label wraps only the icon, so a click beside it in the bar
   does nothing (the CSS review's finding that split the old strip from its label still holds). *@
<label class="drawio-ruler-switch drawio-btn-icon drawio-has-tip">
    <input type="checkbox" id="drawio-ruler-switch" aria-label="Rulers" checked="@Enabled" @onchange="OnChangeAsync" />
    <DrawioIcon Name="rulers" />
    <span class="drawio-tip" role="tooltip">Rulers</span>
</label>

@code {
    [Parameter] public bool Enabled { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public EventCallback<bool> OnToggle { get; set; }

    private Task OnChangeAsync(ChangeEventArgs e) => OnToggle.InvokeAsync(e.Value is true);
}
